From 562882fb757191081f4bce8fe67460184cdf99ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:26:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 035/115] drm/msm/adreno: attach the OPP regulator when the GPU
 wires one up

taimen-v6.0 carries commit 0e6d9faf3bc6 ("drm/msm/a5xx: voltage-scaled
GPU DVFS, full 257-710 MHz range on msm8998"), which wired a GPU core
rail through devm_pm_opp_set_config() so dev_pm_opp_set_rate() scales
voltage with frequency instead of jumping the clock alone. Most of
that commit is already redundant here: msm_gpu.c enable_clk()/
disable_clk() and msm_gpu_devfreq.c msm_devfreq_target() already call
dev_pm_opp_set_rate() instead of a raw clk_set_rate(), and
msm8998.dtsi / msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi already carry the
opp-microvolt ceilings and "vdd-supply = <&pm8005_s1>;" -- the DTS
side landed in an earlier commit on this branch, complete with a
comment pointing at adreno_get_pwrlevels() for the regulator attach.

That attach was the one piece that hadn't actually landed.
adreno_gpu_init() already calls devm_pm_opp_set_clkname() to give the
OPP table its "core" clock, but nothing ever called
devm_pm_opp_set_config()/devm_pm_opp_set_regulators() for the "vdd"
regulator the DT now provides. Without it dev_pm_opp_set_rate() has no
regulator to sequence, so it degenerates to a clock-only rate change:
DT wires vdd_gfx (pm8005 s1) to the OPP table, but nothing ever
attaches it, so DVFS runs the GPU up to 710 MHz at whatever voltage
the bootloader happened to leave the rail at -- the exact
regulator-always-on situation that earlier commit fixed, just with the DT
half now silently inert instead of deleted.

Add the missing half: when the GPU node has "vdd-supply", attach it
via devm_pm_opp_set_regulators() before devm_pm_opp_of_add_table(),
matching the ordering devm_pm_opp_set_config() requires (it WARN_Ons
if the OPP table already has entries). The clk name is left alone --
it's already set elsewhere -- so this only adds the regulator half
that adreno_get_pwrlevels() was missing, rather than reintroducing
that earlier commit's now-redundant clk_names wiring on top of it.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c
index af1041c74287..6530da295c44 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c
@@ -1140,6 +1140,28 @@ static int adreno_get_pwrlevels(struct device *dev,
 
 	gpu->fast_rate = 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * GMU-less GPUs whose core rail is a plain regulator (a540 on
+	 * msm8998: vdd_gfx = pm8005 s1) need the OPP framework to scale
+	 * voltage with frequency -- there is no firmware to do it.
+	 * dev_pm_opp_set_rate() (msm_gpu.c enable_clk()/disable_clk() and
+	 * msm_gpu_devfreq.c msm_devfreq_target() already call it, not a raw
+	 * clk_set_rate()) only sequences volt-then-clk if a regulator is
+	 * attached to the OPP table. The clk side of that attachment is
+	 * already done by devm_pm_opp_set_clkname() in adreno_gpu_init();
+	 * this adds the regulator side when the GPU node wires one up. Must
+	 * run before devm_pm_opp_of_add_table() below -- dev_pm_opp_set_config()
+	 * WARN_Ons if the OPP table already has entries.
+	 */
+	if (of_find_property(dev->of_node, "vdd-supply", NULL)) {
+		static const char * const reg_names[] = { "vdd", NULL };
+
+		ret = devm_pm_opp_set_regulators(dev, reg_names);
+		if (ret)
+			DRM_DEV_ERROR(dev,
+				      "Unable to set OPP regulator: %d\n", ret);
+	}
+
 	/* devm_pm_opp_of_add_table may error out but will still create an OPP table */
 	ret = devm_pm_opp_of_add_table(dev);
 	if (ret == -ENODEV) {
